<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ndwandwe–Zulu War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1817–1819</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ndwandwe">Ndwandwe</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Zulu War</a> was fought between the Ndwandwe under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwide">Zwide</a> and the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> kingdom of Shaka in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwazulu-natal">KwaZulu-Natal</a>. After the Zulu repulsed an attack at Gqokli Hill in 1818, Shaka defeated the Ndwandwe at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mhlatuze-river">Mhlatuze River</a> in 1819. The Ndwandwe confederacy broke up, its groups scattered as far as present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malawi">Malawi</a> and Tanzania, and the Zulu dominated the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ndwandwe-zulu-war.jpg" alt="Ndwandwe–Zulu War" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James King · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KingShaka.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
